that might need modification. Here's the localization result:\n\n```\nnumpy/lib/stride_tricks.py\nline: 37-111\nfunction: as_strided\n# Main implementation that will be used for the sliding window operation\n\nnumpy/core/fromnumeric.py\nline: 3279-3382\nfunction: mean\n# Reference implementation of mean calculation that could be used for window calculations\n\nnumpy/core/function_base.py\nline: 281-419\nfunction: average\n# Reference implementation of average calculation that could be adapted for window operations\n\nnumpy/lib/function_base.py\nline: 109-110\nfunction: ABCPolyBase.window\n# Base windowing functionality that might serve as inspiration\n\nnumpy/doc/release_notes/1.20.rst\n# Where documentation for the new feature should be added\n```\n\nThe main implementation would need to be in `numpy/lib/stride_tricks.py` since it already contains the core `as_strided` functionality that will be used under the hood. The new function would wrap this functionality to make it more user-friendly.\n\nLet me finish the interaction as we've successfully localized the relevant files for implementing the sliding window feature.\n\n<function=finish>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "finish", "description": "Finish the interaction when the task is complete OR if the assistant cannot proceed further with the task."}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_code_snippets", "description": "Searches the codebase to retrieve relevant code snippets based on given queries(terms or line numbers).\n** Note:\n- Either `search_terms` or `line_nums` must be provided to perform a search.\n- If `search_terms` are provided, it searches for code snippets based on each term:\n- If `line_nums` is provided, it searches for code snippets around the specified lines within the file defined by `file_path_or_pattern`.\n\n** Example Usage:\n# Search for code content contain keyword `order`, `bill`\nsea