f there are no floating point input arrays (all integral inputs for\n682 |     instance), return the default floating point dtype for the namespace.\n683 |     \"\"\"\n684 |     dtyped_arrays = [a for a in arrays if hasattr(a, \"dtype\")]\n685 |     floating_dtypes = [\n686 |         a.dtype for a in dtyped_arrays if xp.isdtype(a.dtype, \"real floating\")\n687 |     ]\n688 |     if floating_dtypes:\n689 |         # Return the floating dtype with the highest precision:\n690 |         return xp.result_type(*floating_dtypes)\n691 | \n692 |     # If none of the input arrays have a floating point dtype, they must be all\n693 |     # integer arrays or containers of Python scalars: return the default\n694 |     # floating point dtype for the namespace (implementation specific).\n695 |     return xp.asarray(0.0).dtype\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me also check for the related test file:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['test_regression.py']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nNo results for test files: `test_regression.py`. Please do not search for any test files.\n"}, {"content": "Based on the analysis, here are the key locations that need to be modified to implement the suggested feature:\n\n```\nsklearn/metrics/_regression.py\nline: 58\nline: 97\nfunction: _check_reg_targets\n\nsklearn/utils/_array_api.py\nline: 673\nfunction: _find_matching_floating_dtype\n\nsklearn/utils/_array_api.py\nline: 893\nfunction: indexing_dtype\n\nsklearn/metrics/test_regression.py\nline: 1\nNote: Test file needs updates to validate the new behavior\n\nsklearn/metrics/_regression.py\nline: 100\nline: 101\nfunction: _check_reg_targets\nNote: These lines currently handle array validation, which might need adjustment in the new implementation\n```\n\nThe main changes would involve modifying the `_check_reg_targets` function 