tructor = sp.csr_matrix if X.format == \"csr\" else sp.csc_matrix\n63 |     Xt_sparse = sparse_constructor(\n64 |         (Xt, X.indices.copy(), X.indptr.copy()), shape=X.shape, dtype=bool\n65 |     )\n66 | \n67 |     return Xt_sparse\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me analyze the key information from the problem statement and search results:\n\n1. The feature request is about adding conversion functionality between old and new tags systems.\n2. Key components mentioned:\n   - BaseEstimator's tag system\n   - Estimator classes implementing `_get_tags` or `_more_tags`\n   - `__sklearn_tags__` property\n   - `get_tags` function\n   - Tag validation and checking utilities\n\n3. Let me look deeper into the core files:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sklearn/utils/_tags.py:Tags', 'sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed', 'sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:Tags`...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:Tags`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:Tags`.\n```\n183 | class Tags:\n184 |     \"\"\"Tags for the estimator.\n185 | \n186 |     See :ref:`estimator_tags` for more information.\n187 | \n188 |     Parameters\n189 |     ----------\n190 |     estimator_type : str or None\n191 |         The type of the estimator. Can be one of:\n192 |         - \"classifier\"\n193 |         - \"regressor\"\n194 |         - \"transformer\"\n195 |         - \"clusterer\"\n196 |         - \"outlier_detector\"\n197 |         - \"density_estimator\"\n198 | \n199 |     target_tags : :class:`TargetTags`\n200 |         The target(y) tags.\n201 | \n202 |     transformer_tags : :class:`TransformerTags` or None\n203 |         The transformer tags.\n204 | \n205 |     classifier_tags : :class:`ClassifierTags` or None\n206 |         The classifier tags.\n207 | \n208 |     regressor_tags : :class:`RegressorTags` or None\n209 |         The regressor tags.\n210 | \n211 |     array_api_support : bool, default=False\n212 |         Whether the estimator supports Array API compatible inputs.\n213 | \n214 |     no_validation : bool, default=False\n215 |         Whether the estimator skips input-validation. This is only meant for\n216 |         stateless and dummy transformers!\n217 | \n218 |     non_deterministic : bool, default=False\n219 |         Whether the estimator is not deterministic given a fixed ``random_state``.\n220 | \n221 |     requires_fit : bool, default=True\n222 |         Whether the estimator requires to be fitted before calling one of\n223 |         `transform`, `predict`, `predict_proba`, or `decision_function`.\n224 | \n225 |     _skip_test : bool, default=False\n226 |         Whether to skip common tests entirely. Don't use this unless\n227 |         you have a *very good* reason.\n228 | \n229 |     input_tags : :class:`InputTags`\n230 |         The input data(X) tags.\n231 |     \"\"\"\n232 | \n233 |     estimator_type: str | None\n234 |     target_tags: TargetTags\n235 |     transformer_tags: TransformerTags | None = None\n236 |     classifier_tags: ClassifierTags | None = None\n237 |     regressor_tags: RegressorTags | None = None\n238 |     array_api_support: bool = False\n239 |     no_validation: bool = False\n240 |     non_deterministic: bool = False\n241 |     requires_fit: bool = True\n242 |     _skip_test: bool = False\n243 |     input_tags: InputTags = field(default_factory=InputTags)\n```\n\n\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed`.\n```\n4447 | def check_estimator_tags_renamed(name, estimator_orig):\n4448 |     help = \"\"\"{tags_func}() was removed in 1.6. Please use __sklearn_tags__ instead.\n4449 | You can implement both __sklearn_tags__() and {tags_func}() to support multiple\n4450 | scikit-learn versions.\n4451 | \"\"\"\n4452 | \n4453 |     for klass in type(estimator_orig).mro():\n4454 |         if (\n4455 |             # Here we check vars(...) because we want to check if the method is\n4456 |             # explicitly defined in the class instead of inherited from a parent class.\n4457 |             (\"_more_tags\" in vars(klass) or \"_get_tags\" in vars(klass))\n4458 |             and \"__sklearn_tags__\" not in vars(klass)\n4459 |         ):\n4460 |             raise TypeError(\n4461 |                 f\"Estimator {name} has defined either `_more_tags` or `_get_tags`,\"\n4462 |                 \" but not `__sklearn_tags__`. If you're customizing tags, and need to\"\n4463 |                 \" support multiple scikit-learn versions, you can implement both\"\n4464 |                 \" `__sklearn_tags__` and `_more_tags` or `_get_tags`. This change was\"\n4465 |                 \" introduced in scikit-learn=1.6\"\n4466 |             )\n```\n\n\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\n```\n293 | def get_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n294 |     \"\"\"Get estimator tags.\n295 | \n296 |     :class:`~sklearn.BaseEstimator` provides the estimator tags machinery.\n297 |     However, if an estimator does not inherit from this base class, we should\n298 |     fall-back to the default tags.\n299 | \n300 |     For scikit-learn built-in estimators, we should still rely on\n301 |     `self.__sklearn_tags__()`. `get_tags(est)` should be used when we\n302 |     are not sure where `est` comes from: typically\n303 |     `get_tags(self.estimator)` where `self` is a meta-