n2916 |         zs : float or array-like, default: 0\n2917 |             The z-positions. Either an array of the same length as *xs* and\n2918 |             *ys* or a single value to place all points in the same plane.\n2919 |         zdir : {'x', 'y', 'z', '-x', '-y', '-z'}, default: 'z'\n2920 |             The axis direction for the *zs*. This is useful when plotting 2D\n2921 |             data on a 3D Axes. The data must be passed as *xs*, *ys*. Setting\n2922 |             *zdir* to 'y' then plots the data to the x-z-plane.\n2923 | \n2924 |             See also :doc:`/gallery/mplot3d/2dcollections3d`.\n2925 | \n2926 |         s : float or array-like, default: 20\n2927 |             The marker size in points**2. Either an array of the same length\n2928 |             as *xs* and *ys* or a single value to make all markers the same\n2929 |             size.\n2930 |         c : :mpltype:`color`, sequence, or sequence of colors, optional\n2931 |             The marker color. Possible values:\n2932 | \n2933 |             - A single color format string.\n2934 |             - A sequence of colors of length n.\n2935 |             - A sequence of n numbers to be mapped to colors using *cmap* and\n2936 |               *norm*.\n2937 |             - A 2D array in which the rows are RGB or RGBA.\n2938 | \n2939 |             For more details see the *c* argument of `~.axes.Axes.scatter`.\n2940 |         depthshade : bool, default: True\n2941 |             Whether to shade the scatter markers to give the appearance of\n2942 |             depth. Each call to ``scatter()`` will perform its depthshading\n2943 |             independently.\n2944 |         axlim_clip : bool, default: False\n2945 |             Whether to hide the scatter points outside the axes view limits.\n2946 | \n2947 |             .. versionadded:: 3.10\n2948 |         data : indexable object, optional\n2949 |             DATA_PARAMETER_PLACEHOLDER\n2950 |         **kwargs\n2951 |             All other keyword arguments are passed on to `~.axes.Axes.scatter`.\n2952 | \n2953 |         Returns\n2954 |         -------\n2955 |         paths : `~matplotlib.collections.PathCollection`\n2956 |         \"\"\"\n2957 | \n2958 |         had_data = self.has_data()\n2959 |         zs_orig = zs\n2960 | \n2961 |         xs, ys, zs = cbook._broadcast_with_masks(xs, ys, zs)\n2962 |         s = np.ma.ravel(s)  # This doesn't have to match x, y in size.\n2963 | \n2964 |         xs, ys, zs, s, c, color = cbook.delete_masked_points(\n2965 |             xs, ys, zs, s, c, kwargs.get('color', None)\n2966 |             )\n2967 |         if kwargs.get(\"color\") is not None:\n2968 |             kwargs['color'] = color\n2969 | \n2970 |         # For xs and ys, 2D scatter() will do the copying.\n2971 |         if np.may_share_memory(zs_orig, zs):  # Avoid unnecessary copies.\n2972 |             zs = zs.copy()\n2973 | \n2974 |         patches = super().scatter(xs, ys, s=s, c=c, *args, **kwargs)\n2975 |         art3d.patch_collection_2d_to_3d(patches, zs=zs, zdir=zdir,\n2976 |                                         depthshade=depthshade,\n2977 |                                         axlim_clip=axlim_clip)\n2978 | \n2979 |         if self._zmargin < 0.05 and xs.size > 0:\n2980 |             self.set_zmargin(0.05)\n2981 | \n2982 |         self.auto_scale_xyz(xs, ys, zs, had_data)\n2983 | \n2984 |         return patches\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"scatter()\", \"bar() scatter()\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `lib/matplotlib/pyplot.py:scatter`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n3918 | def scatter(\n3919 |     x: float | ArrayLike,\n3920 |     y: float | ArrayLike,\n3921 |     s: float | ArrayLike | None = None,\n3922 |     c: ArrayLike | Sequence[ColorType] | ColorType | None = None,\n3923 |     marker: MarkerType | None = None,\n3924 |     cmap: str | Colormap | None = None,\n3925 |     norm: str | Normalize | None = None,\n3926 |     vmin: float | None = None,\